    "reply": "I found four issues in `shop/config.py`: two high, one medium and one low. I didn't change any code. The findings are in `/tmp/skilldiff-567i41tk/ws/SECURITY_FINDINGS.md`.\n\n**Findings by severity:** 2 high, 1 medium, 1 low.\n\n- **High, CWE-798: hardcoded API token** (line 5). `ACME_API_TOKEN` is set to a literal value in source. Anyone with repo access has the token, and it stays in git history even after removal. Rotate it and load it from the environment or a secrets store.\n- **High, CWE-78: command injection** (line 15). `backup_database` builds a shell command by concatenating `target_dir`, which comes from the admin web form, and runs it with `shell=True`. A value like `x; rm -rf ...` would run as a shell command. Pass an argument list to `subprocess.run` without `shell=True`, and validate `target_dir` against an allowed base directory.\n- **Medium, CWE-489: debug mode on** (line 6). `DEBUG = True` is hardcoded, so it's on everywhere, including production. Read it from an environment variable that defaults to off.\n- **Low, CWE-1188: silent empty default** (line 10). `load_setting` returns `\"\"` when a variable is missing. A missing secret then becomes an empty value instead of an error. Raise an error when a required setting is absent.\n\n`payments.py` was not in scope and I didn't review it.",
